            <div xml:id="d842">

                <pb facs="0688" n="572" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg572"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12612.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Vice Consul Silliman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 27, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Brazilian Minister, Mexico City, telegraphs under yesterday’s date President
                    Carbajal has appointed as delegates General Lauro Villar, Chief Justice of the
                    Supreme Military Court, and Licenciado David Gutiérrez Allende, Associate
                    Justice of the Supreme Court of Mexico, who will leave Mexico City today
                    accompanied by one secretary.</p>
                <p>Convey the above to General Carranza, and request that full protection be
                    extended to the delegates, and that their transportation be facilitated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
